From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:44:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: map a writable i386 section view over its whole host
 pages

An i386 child's data section view is claimed in its window as whole
16 KiB host pages, but it was mapped with the view's own size. For a
section that is not a multiple of a host page (FMOD Ex's semaphores
are 0x14-byte pagefile-backed sections) map_file_into_view_ex then saw
a mapping that ends before its view, refused it as an unaligned shared
mapping, and MapViewOfFile returned NULL with ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER;
BioShock's FMOD thread close then crashed on a NULL semaphore. Map a
writable view over all of its host pages, as the host's mmap does for
a native view: one shared mapping, so every view of the section and of
a duplicated handle aliases. The server still registers the view's own
size. Read-only and write-copy views keep their copy fallback.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-13-small-shared-sections.md
Offered-upstream: no; the window exists only on the iOS port
---
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
index 5537a30..3f03de8 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
@@ -15542,7 +15542,12 @@ static NTSTATUS ios_wow64_map_file_view( uintptr_t window, HANDLE mapping, void
     if (!status) status = ios_wow64_claim_view( window, guest, length, vprot, &view );
     if (!status)
     {
-        status = map_file_into_view_ex( view, unix_fd, 0, size, offset, vprot, needs_close, FALSE );
+        /* A writable view must be one shared mapping, and the view is whole host
+         * pages: map the section over all of them, as the host's mmap does for a
+         * native view. The part past the view's size is the rest of the section,
+         * or zeros past its end within the last host page. */
+        status = map_file_into_view_ex( view, unix_fd, 0, (vprot & VPROT_WRITE) ? length : size, offset,
+                                        vprot, needs_close, FALSE );
         if (!status)
         {
             SERVER_START_REQ( map_view )
